    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0693" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the British Foreign
                        Secretary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eden</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d290-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-11">August 11, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret to Winant for Eden from the President.</p>
                <p>I fully approve Former Naval Person’s proposed reply to Badoglio’s emissary Berio
                    in Tangier as recommended by you.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d290-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f2" n="2" xml:id="d290-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>. Eden sent the approved instructions to
                    Tangier on August 13, 1943, on which date a copy of them was sent to Hull by the
                    British Embassy at Washington (740.00119 European War 1939/1578).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
